1
00:00:01,030 --> 00:00:03,120
<i>Over ten years ago,</i>

2
00:00:03,430 --> 00:00:08,400
<i>a series of gates linking our world
to an alternate dimension appeared.</i>

3
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:14,560
<i>The other side of each gate teemed
with bizarre creatures called "magic beasts,"</i>

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,990
<i>immune to conventional weaponry.</i>

5
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:20,720
<i>Those who have awakened the abilities
necessary to fight these beasts</i>

6
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:22,750
<i>are called hunters.</i>

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,460
<i>Based on the amount of magical power
contained within their bodies,</i>

8
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:33,870
<i>they are ranked, in descending order,
as S, A, B, C, D, or E-Rank.</i>

9
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:39,870
<i>However, once these powers have awakened,
no amount of individual effort</i>

10
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,610
<i>can ever result in greater strength.</i>

11
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:48,730
<i>The one who awoke to the weakest level
of strength, even among the E-Ranks,</i>

12
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:50,620
<i>was me, Sung Jinwoo.</i>

13
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:56,790
<i>Having become "The Weakest Hunter of
All Mankind," I was always a hindrance,</i>

14
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:58,530
<i>and always on the verge of death.</i>

15
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,430
<i>There are only a handful of
S-Rank hunters in the country.</i>

16
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:06,130
<i>I wish I could've been like them.</i>

17
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:11,550
<i>And overseeing those hunters,
as well as managing dungeon raids,</i>

18
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:13,090
<i>is the Hunter's Association.</i>

19
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:18,820
<i>They're unfathomably strong.
And they fight together.</i>

20
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:22,190
<i>People who help each other,
are useful, and support each other.</i>

21
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:27,730
<i>The kind of person that someone as
helpless and useless as I could never be.</i>

22
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:32,870
<i>That's what I thought...
until everything changed.</i>

23
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,950
Hey, it's Sung!

24
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,390
What's up, Sung?

25
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:19,920
<i>I'm Sung Jinwoo, and even among
the weakest of all ranks,</i>

26
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:17,640
Nice of you to come out despite
the chilly weather.

27
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:22,600
<i>I had earned a certain nickname...</i>

28
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:25,600
His nickname is "The Weakest
Hunter of All Mankind."

29
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:31,280
<i>But even if I was the weakest of all mankind,
I had a family to protect.</i>

30
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:29,820
Let's give it our best.

31
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,170
Today, I'm gonna see this through!

32
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:36,530
<i>I needed to help beat the dungeons on the
other side of the gates and earn a living.</i>

33
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:41,160
I did it!

34
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,270
I finally got one.

35
00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:44,300
Jinwoo!

36
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,180
Jinwoo!

37
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,510
Stay back, Joohee!

38
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:11,790
You're going to be okay!
I promise I'll heal you!

39
00:04:23,110 --> 00:04:24,330
All right!

40
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:26,200
That's Mr. Song for you!

41
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,870
Hey!

42
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:29,620
Take a look at this!

43
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:33,590
<i>After clearing the dungeon, further in,
we discovered it was a double dungeon—</i>

44
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,590
I'm in!

45
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:34,910
I say no.

46
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:38,070
<i>if we took on the risk, we'd have the chance
to earn even greater rewards.</i>

47
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:36,220
No.

48
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:39,980
<i>I'm the only one who can
provide for my family.</i>

49
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:42,140
<i>We took a vote, and the majority
decided to keep going.</i>

50
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,720
Let's go.

51
00:04:49,270 --> 00:04:52,400
<i>And that was a mistake.</i>

52
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,380
Everybody, get down!

53
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:09,540
<i>What is happening here?</i>

54
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:12,250
<i>How is this possible?</i>

55
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:15,210
<i>We're trapped. We're done for.</i>

56
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:17,670
<i>We're dead. Dead.</i>

57
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,760
<i>We're gonna die!</i>

58
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:33,400
<i>We were absolutely helpless against
the boss of the double dungeon.</i>

59
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:31,810
I can't... I can't do this!

60
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,830
I can't die just yet!

61
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:38,280
<i>We had no choice but to wait for death.</i>

62
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:38,280
I wanna make it home alive!

63
00:05:41,890 --> 00:05:44,450
Mr. Song. Take Joohee and go.

64
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,080
I just said I'm going to stay—

65
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:49,560
Then who's going to carry Joohee out?

66
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,340
There's no time. Hurry!

67
00:05:52,510 --> 00:05:54,020
You can't, Jinwoo!

68
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,130
In that case, it should be me—

69
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:57,920
I promised to take you out to eat, didn't I?

70
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:00,430
Use this to buy yourself dinner.

71
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,830
And when I get out of here,
I'll be along to collect the change.

72
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:05,340
How can you even say—

73
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:11,670
I'm sorry. But it looks like
we really are out of time.

74
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:12,870
Please.

75
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:23,700
<i>Good. I'm the only one who has to die.</i>

76
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:33,660
I'll take at least one of you down with me...

77
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,100
So bring it on!

78
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:50,120
<i>I've always been the weakest.</i>

79
00:06:50,630 --> 00:06:52,970
<i>And I've been mocked for it,
time and time again.</i>

80
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:55,660
<i>But I've always tried as hard as I could.</i>

81
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,110
<i>And now...</i>

82
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:03,570
<i>This is bullshit.</i>

83
00:07:04,270 --> 00:07:06,560
<i>It's bullshit! This is such bullshit!</i>

84
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:11,200
<i>I tried to be stronger...</i>

85
00:07:12,210 --> 00:07:14,160
<i>but I couldn't.</i>

86
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:23,590
<i>And even then,
I gave it my all to get this far!</i>

87
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:34,370
<i>You couldn't take any more?
We all felt the same way!</i>

88
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:37,040
<i>All you were doing was
justifying your own selfishness!</i>

89
00:07:39,870 --> 00:07:42,470
<i>That gratitude was purely superficial.</i>

90
00:07:42,470 --> 00:07:46,950
<i>It's always the most selfish
people who benefit the most!</i>

91
00:07:47,330 --> 00:07:51,450
<i>I have a family, too!
I wanted to make it home alive, too!</i>

92
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:01,380
<i>It's good that I'm the only one
who has to die?</i>

93
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:11,120
<i>How could you think that,
you stupid hypocrite?</i>

94
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:18,140
<i>No. I don't wanna die.</i>

95
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:28,450
<i>If... If I had one more chance...</i>

96
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:58,150
<i>When I woke up, I was in a hospital bed,</i>

97
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:55,800
<i>A hospital?</i>

98
00:08:58,470 --> 00:09:04,320
<i>and the limbs that I had lost were back
like nothing had happened.</i>

99
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,270
<i>My arm's intact.</i>

100
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,320
<i>My legs, too.</i>

101
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:08,510
<i>And that wasn't the only strange thing.</i>

102
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:13,120
<i>For some reason, there were these things
like message windows from a game</i>

103
00:09:11,890 --> 00:09:14,400
But, Jinah... Can you see this?

104
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,770
<i>that only I could see.</i>

105
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,770
See what?

106
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:17,340
Never mind. Sorry.

107
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:22,350
<i>It's been four days since
I regained consciousness.</i>

108
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,080
<i>I've figured out a few things.</i>

109
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:28,310
<i>First, I'm not hallucinating these windows.</i>

110
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:32,860
<i>When I complete the daily quest,
I get three types of rewards.</i>

111
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:34,520
Full recovery.

112
00:09:35,870 --> 00:09:38,200
All that exhaustion is gone in a flash.

113
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:42,300
Next is the ability points.

114
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:45,440
<i>I can distribute the points
into whatever abilities I choose.</i>

115
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:47,840
<i>I should probably go with strength, right?</i>

116
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:51,500
<i>Upgrading my abilities makes me
that much more powerful.</i>

117
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,570
<i>I can literally tell that
I've got more strength now.</i>

118
00:09:55,920 --> 00:10:00,000
<i>And my final daily quest reward...
the random loot box.</i>

119
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,800
<i>I wonder what it'll be today?</i>

120
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:10,350
A key?

121
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:16,700
An instance dungeon? What's that?

122
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:23,270
Based on what's happened so far, it'll be
some kind of event to help me get stronger...

123
00:10:37,490 --> 00:10:41,200
What do I do? I'm suddenly
feeling less confident.

124
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:48,630
Here they come! And there's three!

125
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:07,790
<i>I beat one...</i>

126
00:11:36,190 --> 00:11:38,200
It doesn't look anything
like the station I know.

127
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:46,070
<i>So fast!</i>

128
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:51,820
<i>The sword...</i>

129
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:02,180
<i>Even after all that leveling up,
its name is still...</i>

130
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:05,000
<i>orange?</i>

131
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:10,130
<i>If it lands a clean hit on me, I'm dead.</i>

132
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:33,290
<i>I thought I'd gotten a bit stronger...</i>

133
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:45,490
<i>Is it still not enough?</i>

134
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:49,640
<i>How much stronger do I need to get...</i>

135
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:54,740
<i>before it makes up for a life
spent being a laughing stock?</i>

136
00:13:12,350 --> 00:13:13,860
I've...

137
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:21,930
gotta get stronger!

138
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:29,370
<i>Not yet!</i>

139
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:34,490
<i>Compared to that thing...
Compared to the terror I felt back then...</i>

140
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:37,000
<i>This will be easy!</i>

141
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:54,940
<i>I focused specifically
on increasing my strength!</i>

142
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,650
<i>I should be able to...</i>

143
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:07,780
I know that, here and now,

144
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:12,540
I can kill you!

145
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:38,360
Oh my gosh, did you see him?

146
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:41,810
<i>After awakening, your ability
values are set and don't change.</i>

147
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,570
I sure did! You mean the E-Rank, right?

148
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:46,440
<i>But for some reason...
I'm the only person that can level up.</i>

149
00:14:42,630 --> 00:14:43,740
Excuse me.

150
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,910
Mr. Sung Jinwoo...

151
00:14:47,750 --> 00:14:50,540
Oh, sorry.

152
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:54,480
And you seem taller.
Did the exercise help with that, too?

153
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,940
<i>This would help me earn
way more money than before.</i>

154
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:58,140
I guess men keep growing
even when they're adults!

155
00:14:55,590 --> 00:14:57,220
<i>Or so I thought...</i>

156
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:01,000
That said... It's not exactly easy, either.

157
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:05,350
To make good money, I need to go
through higher-ranked gates.

158
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:10,360
But no one's gonna let an
E-Rank hunter into those.

159
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:12,810
Maybe I could get re-appraised?

160
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:16,070
A higher rank could get me into better gates,

161
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:18,480
and maybe a bit of attention
will help me earn more...

162
00:15:19,370 --> 00:15:23,940
<i>I'd definitely stand out, though.
Re-awakenings are rare enough.</i>

163
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:28,920
<i>I've never heard of a hunter who could
level up and keep getting stronger.</i>

164
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:32,240
<i>Which would probably mean even more scrutiny.</i>

165
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:36,840
<i>The press would eat it up... and there's
the saying about the nail that sticks out.</i>

166
00:15:37,450 --> 00:15:38,740
<i>I better not.</i>

167
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:45,000
<i>Not until I can properly defend myself
and learn what the deal is with this power.</i>

168
00:15:56,950 --> 00:15:58,020
Confirm.

169
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:00,920
Hey, there!

170
00:16:04,010 --> 00:16:05,340
I'm Hwang Dongsuk.

171
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:06,520
Sung Jinwoo.

172
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,780
You're E-Rank, right?

173
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:08,410
Right.

174
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:11,680
It looks like we're here for the same reason.

175
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:15,270
I'm Yoo Jinho. Twenty-one years old, D-Rank.

176
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:17,360
I'm here to meet the quota, too.

177
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:22,800
<i>A D-Rank with gear like that?
This kid's family must be rich.</i>

178
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:25,840
Is this your first time in a C-Rank dungeon?

179
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,840
It's okay! I'll keep you safe.

180
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:34,850
Let's be on our way!

181
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,260
Good! Now, let's wrap this up!

182
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:39,390
Hell yeah!

183
00:16:40,630 --> 00:16:42,090
<i>They're well coordinated.</i>

184
00:16:42,090 --> 00:16:45,350
<i>It's easy to see that they've been
working together for a long time.</i>

185
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:50,490
<i>Still, it might be the lack of a healer,
but they're a bit rough around the edges.</i>

186
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:52,160
<i>Something...</i>

187
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,370
<i>feels off.</i>

188
00:16:57,390 --> 00:17:01,830
Kyuhwan... seal off the boss chamber.

189
00:16:58,250 --> 00:17:00,320
<i>My hunch was right.</i>

190
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,880
<i>A seasoned party that needed
extra members to meet the quota...</i>

191
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,590
The entrance! But why?

192
00:17:04,210 --> 00:17:05,590
<i>One with no healers.</i>

193
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:11,460
<i>Hwang Dongsuk had been hiring low-ranked
hunters to meet the entrance quota,</i>

194
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:16,340
<i>and then killing them in the dungeon
to monopolize the rewards.</i>

195
00:17:18,230 --> 00:17:23,190
<i>Their plan was to trap me and Jinho
in the boss chamber and let us die.</i>

196
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:28,690
<i>But because I beat the boss,
their plan was in shambles.</i>

197
00:17:29,150 --> 00:17:32,320
<i>So they tried to kill us.</i>

198
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,160
<i>Enemies...</i>

199
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:45,040
<i>The system is telling me to kill.</i>

200
00:17:45,590 --> 00:17:48,380
<i>The system wants me alive.</i>

201
00:17:52,930 --> 00:17:54,780
<i>It wants me strong.</i>

202
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:58,090
I'd forgotten.

203
00:17:58,850 --> 00:18:02,880
The weak always get taken from.
That's how it works here.

204
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:07,340
Hey, look! The Weakest Hunter
of All Mankind actually gets it!

205
00:18:07,830 --> 00:18:12,440
That means you guys understand
how it works, too, right?

206
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:15,140
How what works?

207
00:18:15,490 --> 00:18:17,520
If you're hunters...

208
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:23,040
then you're ready to be
preyed on yourselves, right?

209
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:27,210
Let me handle this, Mr. Dongsuk.

210
00:18:27,210 --> 00:18:31,670
Look, buddy. You clearly don't
understand what's going on here.

211
00:18:32,070 --> 00:18:34,150
We should be ready to be preyed on?

212
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:37,690
And what's a jumped-up
E-Rank like you gonna do?

213
00:18:37,690 --> 00:18:39,890
The Weakest Hunter of All—

214
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:56,440
<i>I just killed someone.</i>

215
00:18:56,990 --> 00:18:58,300
<i>A human being.</i>

216
00:18:58,830 --> 00:19:01,730
<i>Even if I was just obeying the system,</i>

217
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:06,370
<i>I've... just murdered another person.</i>

218
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:10,200
<i>But if I hadn't done it, I would've died.</i>

219
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:12,890
<i>So I can't back down now.</i>

220
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:17,470
<i>If only the strong get to survive, then...!</i>

221
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:19,720
Go to hell!

222
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,940
How's an E-Rank got moves like that?

223
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,120
Son of a bitch...

224
00:19:46,990 --> 00:19:48,250
Take this!

225
00:19:56,490 --> 00:19:57,590
He's so strong...

226
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:02,560
He feels stronger now than when
he was fighting the dungeon boss.

227
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:05,580
H-He took my entire team apart in seconds...

228
00:20:06,170 --> 00:20:08,270
Was he hiding his true strength?

229
00:20:08,570 --> 00:20:10,800
You beat the boss, didn't you?

230
00:20:11,770 --> 00:20:15,860
Well, I might be a C-Rank, too,
but you'll find I'm nothing like them!

231
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:17,700
Reinforcement!

232
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:27,580
Mr. Hwang. You're strong.

233
00:20:28,710 --> 00:20:31,340
But I've got some bad news for you.

234
00:20:36,130 --> 00:20:39,720
I've been leveling up this entire time.

235
00:20:41,060 --> 00:20:43,370
<i>Wh-What just happened?</i>

236
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:46,560
<i>He... He smashed me into the ground?</i>

237
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:50,810
<i>There's no way in hell he's E-Rank!</i>

238
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:53,980
H-Hang on! Don't kill me!

239
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:56,470
You've gotta show mercy! I-I can pay you!

240
00:20:56,470 --> 00:21:00,360
The mana crystals and essence stones...
You can have the lot!

241
00:21:01,150 --> 00:21:04,120
I-Is that not enough for you?
I-In that case...

242
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:06,920
I'll pay you double! Double what I was—

243
00:21:05,810 --> 00:21:06,920
Three times.

244
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:10,580
You tried to kill me three times...

245
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:13,330
and now you want mercy?

246
00:21:13,330 --> 00:21:17,420
D-Don't do it!
Y-You won't get away with this!

247
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:23,090
Weren't you the one who said nothing
that happens in a dungeon ever gets out?

248
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:27,480
You little shit! Do you have
any idea who my brother—

249
00:21:39,010 --> 00:21:40,570
<i>I've become strong.</i>

250
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:47,150
<i>For the people I love, I'll make
any sacrifice to get stronger.</i>

251
00:21:48,330 --> 00:21:51,660
<i>Whether it's against magic beasts or humans,</i>

252
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:58,500
<i>I can't stop fighting.</i>

253
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,580
<i>I have to keep...</i>

254
00:22:06,770 --> 00:22:08,980
<i>leveling up.</i>
